  "agent": {
    "note": "candidate-001 feedback applied. ROOT CAUSE: the nested table drew its OWN card surface, so its edges didn't match the beat's chrome panels (header/rail/footer, which are beat-drawn with a ±pad inset). FIX: the table is now TRANSPARENT (backgroundColor black@0) and the BEAT draws its backdrop — so ALL panels (table / rail / header / footer) share the same ±pad inset and aligned edges. (The table's row washes now blend against a solid base regardless, so the banded rows stay visible with no self-surface; standalone table output is unchanged — washBase==cardBg for a solid bg.) RESULT: (1) desktop — the rail (Total Commits…) panel top/bottom now line up with the table panel; (2) mobile — the table (stacked-card) panel now matches the header section width. Renders: /tmp/b3d3.mp4 (desktop), /tmp/b3s3.mp4 (square), /tmp/b3m3.mp4 (mobile).",
    "question": "Alignment good now on desktop + mobile? Square OK too? Any remaining nudges before I lock Beat 3?",
    "response": {
      "body": "i think the BG color of this leaderboard is too dark.  The vs last week text becomes too small in mobile mode. in general the KPI cards have small text size.\n\nDesktop is the one I'm most comfortable with as is, but still KPI text could be a bit bigger.\n\nIn general its like I want the KPI cards to have bigger font size",
      "from": "human",
      "at": "2026-06-25T01:54:21.783Z",
